# Production build-time config, loaded automatically by `vite build`.
#
# Deliberately relative. The console is served from a different origin to the
# API, and two things follow from that if the browser talks to the API directly:
#
#   1. The deployed API keeps an ALLOWED_ORIGINS allowlist and answers 500 —
#      not a clean CORS rejection — for anything outside it. The Vercel origin
#      is not on that list, so every request failed.
#   2. Its auth cookies would be cross-site, needing SameSite=None; Secure.
#
# vercel.json rewrites /api/v1/* to the API instead, so the browser only ever
# sees one origin. No CORS, no cross-site cookies, and nothing to change on the
# backend.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api/v1
